/4/47/2_mid_temple_8.JPG/960px-2_mid_temple_8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tugu Keris","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.036427,"lo":101.444404,"d":7181,"ds":"Tugu Keris (Kris Monument) is a huge monument in the shape of a kris in Klang, Selangor, Malaysia. Its construction was ordered by the Sultan of Selangor, Almarhum Sultan Salahuddin Abdul Aziz Shah to commemorate the Silver Jubilee of his reign on 30 September 1985. The monument is located at Klang Royal Gardens, opposite the Church of Our Lady of Lourdes Klang.","wpu":"Tugu Keris","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tugu_Keris%2C_Klang.jpg/960px-Tugu_Keris%2C_Klang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Istana Alam Shah","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.033333,"lo":101.45,"d":7527,"ds":"The Istana Alam Shah is the official palace of the Sultan of Selangor, located in southern Klang, the royal town of the state of Selangor, Malaysia.","wpu":"Istana Alam Shah","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Sultan-klang.jpg/960px-Sultan-klang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sultan Sulaiman Mosque","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.034722,"lo":101.450278,"d":7631,"ds":"Sultan Sulaiman Royal Mosque (Malay: Masjid Diraja Sultan Sulaiman) is Selangor's royal mosque, which is located in Klang, Selangor, Malaysia. It was constructed by the British in the early 1922 and was officially opened in 1923 by the late Almarhum Sultan Sir Alaeddin Sulaiman Shah.","wpu":"Sultan Sulaiman Mosque","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/The_Exterior_of_Masjid_Diraja_Sultan_Suleiman.jpg/960px-The_Exterior_of_Masjid_Diraja_Sultan_Suleiman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kota Raja Mahadi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.045194,"lo":101.444889,"d":7814,"ds":"Kota Raja Mahadi is a Malaysian historic defensive fort built by Raja Mahadi on top of Bukit Kota, Klang, Selangor, built in 1860.It was used as the main battle station for him during the Selangor civil war against Raja Abdullah bin Raja Jaafar and later Tengku Kudin.","wpu":"Kota Raja Mahadi","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/SMS0634_Klang_MPK_Kota_Raja_Mahdi_1293_side_s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Sultan Abdul Aziz Royal Gallery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.041306,"lo":101.449194,"d":7927,"ds":"The Sultan Abdul Aziz Royal Gallery (Malay: Galeri Diraja Sultan Abdul Aziz) is a gallery about the former Selangor Sultan Salahuddin Abdul Aziz Shah in Klang District, Selangor, Malaysia. The Royal Gallery is currently chaired by then nephew of Salahuddin of Selangor, Tengku Indera Pahlawan Diraja Selangor (Yang Amat Dihormati Tengku Dato' Setia Putra Alhaj bin Tengku Azman Shah Alhaj).","wpu":"Sultan Abdul Aziz Royal Gallery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sultan_Abdul_Aziz_Royal_Gallery_%28211027%29.jpg/960px-Sultan_Abdul_Aziz_Royal_Gallery_%28211027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Klang Royal Town Mosque","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":3.04775,"lo":101.445778,"d":8073,"ds":"The Klang Royal Town Mosque (Malay: Masjid Bandar Diraja Klang) is a mosque in Klang, Selangor, Malaysia. The mosque is located at Jalan Pasar on the banks of the Klang River giving the image of a floating mosque.","wpu":"Klang Royal Town Mosque","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Floating_Mosque_of_Klang_%288216640379%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Floating_Mosque_of_Klang_%288216640379%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pulau Indah","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":2.948889,"lo":101.331667,"d":8701,"ds":"Pulau Indah (\"Beautiful Island\", formerly known as Pulau Lumut) is an island in Klang District, Selangor, Malaysia with a population of around 20,000 people overall. Malaysia's largest port, West Port, Port Klang, is on the island.","wpu":"Pulau Indah","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Aerial_of_Selangor_2023_18.jpg/960px-Aerial_of_Selangor_2023_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Kuala Lumpur (KL), officially the Federal Territory of Kuala Lumpur, is the capital city and a federal territory of Malaysia. It is the most populous city in the country, covering an area of 243 km2 (94 sq mi) with a population of 2,111,536 as of 2026. Greater Kuala Lumpur, which itself includes the Klang Valley, is an urban agglomeration of 8.81 million people as of 2024.","wpu":"Kuala Lumpur","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Bukit_Bintang_junction_in_2024_2.jpg/960px-Bukit_Bintang_junction_in_2024_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}